# Declared non-bindings: a repository that deliberately does not bind a shimmed
# hook, with the reason.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS.
#
# Once an absent shim is reported rather than skipped, a deliberate opt-out and
# an accidental deletion look identical to the instrument. Without this file it
# must report both or neither, and reporting neither is what the previous
# behaviour chose — the failure that let five repositories carry unmarked inlined
# copies unreported.
#
# An opt-out is reported AS an opt-out, with its reason, and does not count as a
# finding. It is never silence: a hook nobody binds on purpose is still a fact
# about the fleet, and the next migration that re-adds the registration should
# meet the reason before it meets the file.
#
# THE REASON MUST SURVIVE THIS FILE. A rationale kept only in another
# repository's declaration is one `git clone` away from being lost — the live
# instance below had already been manually reverted about three times when it was
# carried as a comment inside the file it justified. So a row is either
# self-contained, or it points at the project's own ADR. It is not required to be
# both: requiring an ADR for a one-sentence fact produces ninety lines of prose
# arguing what the row already says, which is its own kind of loss.
#
# A REASON IS PER HOOK. "This repository is the authority, not a consumer"
# explains why a repository is not a consumer and says nothing about the hook
# being excused. A reason should be specific enough to argue with.
#
# Format: <repo> <hook> <reason>. One per line, blank lines and # ignored.

agenticapps-workflow-core database-sentinel core holds no database credentials, no .env and no deployment secrets — the hook guards a class of file this repository does not contain, so binding it would score an empty set green
